meta {
  name: AMC
  type: http
  seq: 5
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/method/implementor.client_api.get_amc?project=PROJ-0030
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

params:query {
  project: PROJ-0030
  ~customer: Hamza
}

tests {
  test("returns 200", function () {
    expect(res.status).to.equal(200);
  });

  test("has message", function () {
    expect(res.body).to.have.property("message");
  });

  test("has AMC fields only", function () {
    const a = res.body.message;
    expect(a.kind).to.equal("amc");
    expect(a.status).to.equal("amc");
    expect(a).to.have.property("hours_included");
    expect(a.contract_status).to.be.oneOf(["active", "expiring", "expired", null]);
    expect(a.tickets).to.have.property("open");
    expect(a).to.not.have.property("stage");
    expect(a).to.not.have.property("health");
    expect(a).to.not.have.property("percent");
  });
}

settings {
  encodeUrl: true
  timeout: 0
}

docs {
  One AMC contract: period, status, hours used and tickets.

  **Endpoint:** `GET /api/method/implementor.client_api.get_amc`  
  **Screen:** AMC details

  **Permission:** Signed-in client user (Client User or Client Admin). Only records of the user's own client company are returned.

  **Query parameters:**

  | Field | Type | Required | Example | Notes |
  | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
  | `project` | string | yes | `PROJ-0030` | AMC project `name`. |
  | `customer` | string | no | `Hamza` | Not used by the app. The server picks the user's company. Disabled by default. |

  **Response:** the same fields as an AMC item from `get_services` or `get_projects`.

  ```json
  {
    "message": {
      "name": "PROJ-0030",
      "title": "AMC - Hamza Trading",
      "display_title": "AMC",
      "kind": "amc",
      "status": "amc",
      "start_date": "2026-01-01",
      "end_date": "2026-12-31",
      "days_left": 55,
      "project_manager": "Sahana",
      "contract_status": "active",
      "elapsed_percent": 85,
      "hours_used": 18.5,
      "hours_included": 40,
      "tickets": { "open": 2, "closed": 9 }
    }
  }
  ```

  **Fields:**

  - `display_title`: show this, not `title`.
  - `contract_status`: drives the chip. `active`, `expiring` (30 days or less left) or `expired`. Null when the contract has no end date.
  - `status`: always `amc`. Don't use it for the chip.
  - `end_date`: the contract's expected end date, or its deadline when no end date is set.
  - `days_left`: days until `end_date`. Negative once expired. Null when there is no end date.
  - `elapsed_percent`: how much of the contract period has passed, 0 to 100. Use it for the period bar. Null without a start or end date.
  - `hours_used`: hours logged on the contract's tasks (number, up to 2 decimals).
  - `hours_included`: contracted hours. Null when not set (or 0).
  - `tickets`: `open` and `closed` counts for this contract, across the whole company. `open` includes resolved tickets waiting for confirmation.
  - There is no `stage`, `phase`, `health`, `percent`, `go_live_date` or `next_milestone` for an AMC.

  **Payment milestones:** not in this response. Call Milestones with the same `project`. It returns milestones with `display_state` and `can_sign_off`, the same as for implementations. Only the AMC's own milestones are returned, never those from its implementation phase; an AMC with no AMC milestone returns an empty list.

  **Errors:** client API errors have an `error_code`; auth errors raised by Frappe don't.

  - **401** (no error_code): token expired or invalid. Refresh once and retry, else sign out.
  - **403** (no error_code): no Authorization header sent.
  - **403** `not_permitted`: not this client's project, or the project doesn't exist.
  - **403** `no_client_linked`: the user isn't linked to any client company.
  - **417** `not_amc_project`: the project is an implementation. Open it with Implementation instead.
  - **417** `missing_parameter`: `project` left out.

  **Notes:**

  - Hours: when `hours_included` is set, show a used/included bar ("18.5 of 40 hrs"). When it is null, show "18.5 hrs used" alone.
}
